      "subsections": {
        "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS",
          "canonical_heading": "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Lysosomal storage diseases—diffuse diseases of the CNS; differentiate by presence of signs of involvement of parts of the CNS",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "outside of the cerebellum.",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Toxicity (e.g., hexachlorophene)—differentiate by history of",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "exposure.",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Inflammatory diseases—infectious (e.g., canine distemper and feline infectious peritonitis [FIP]) and immune-mediated (dogs). Differentiate from cerebellar degeneration by MRI and cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) analysis. Infectious diseases are frequently accompanied or preceded by",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "systemic signs of illness.",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cerebellar cyst— differentiate by advanced imaging (MRI).",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Medulloblastoma (cerebellar tumor)— reported in dogs and cats <1 year old; differentiate by advanced imaging (MRI) and",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "CSF analysis.",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Other primary and metastatic tumors in adult dogs.",
              "pdf_page": 329,
              "printed_page": 247,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
